# Installing WordPress Agent Skills for OpenAI Codex

This guide explains how to install and use the official WordPress agent skills (`SKILL.md` modules) in OpenAI Codex.

## Prerequisites

* OpenAI Codex (CLI or Desktop App) installed on your machine.
* Node.js **20.18+** (required if using the `npx` CLI installation methods).
* Git (required if cloning the repository manually).

---

## Method 1: Quick Install via CLI (Recommended)

You can install individual skills directly into your project or Codex environment using `npx`.

### Using the `skills` CLI

Run the following command in your terminal, replacing `<skill-name>` with the specific WordPress skill you want to add:

```bash
npx skills add wordpress/agent-skills --skill <skill-name>
```

**Examples:**

```bash
npx skills add wordpress/agent-skills --skill wp-playground
npx skills add wordpress/agent-skills --skill wp-block-development
```

### Using Skills Hub CLI

Alternatively, run the Skills Hub installer inside your project directory to download the `SKILL.md` file and track it in a `.skills.json` lockfile:

```bash
npx @skills-hub-ai/cli install <skill-slug>
```

---

## Method 2: Manual Global Installation

To make all official WordPress skills available across every project on your machine, copy them into your global Codex skills folder.

1. **Create the Codex skills directory** (if it does not already exist):

   ```bash
   mkdir -p ~/.codex/skills
   ```

2. **Clone the official WordPress Agent Skills repository** into a temporary folder and copy the skill folders over:

   ```bash
   git clone https://github.com/WordPress/agent-skills.git /tmp/wp-skills
   cp -r /tmp/wp-skills/skills/* ~/.codex/skills/
   rm -rf /tmp/wp-skills
   ```

   > **Note:** If you have configured a custom `CODEX_HOME` environment variable, copy the folders to `$CODEX_HOME/skills/` instead.

3. **Restart Codex** (CLI session or Desktop App) to detect and load the new skills.

